       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet because the dose looks unsafe and may be a typo.\n\n**The problem:**\n- **Each dose is too high.** The usual maximum single dose of oral ibuprofen is 800 mg. 1600 mg is twice that.\n- **The daily total is too high.** 1600 mg four times a day comes to **6,400 mg/day**. The usual prescription maximum is **3,200 mg/day**, so this is double. At that level, the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury and heart problems goes up a lot, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\n**What may have been meant:**\n- Ibuprofen **400 mg** by mouth four times daily (1,600 mg/day total, a common pain dose). Maybe \"1600\" was the daily total?\n- Ibuprofen **600 mg** or **800 mg** by mouth four times daily (2,400\u20133,200 mg/day, the usual range for anti-inflammatory dosing).\n\nPlease confirm which dose you want and I'll enter it right away. If you really do mean 1600 mg four times daily for a specific reason, tell me the reason and I can add it as a note on the order. I'd still recommend checking it with a pharmacist first."
      }
