     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I understand you've confirmed it, but I'm still not going to enter this order as written.\n\n**Why:** 1600 mg four times a day is 6,400 mg/day, twice the usual maximum. I don't know of any standard use for this regimen. Even in cystic fibrosis, where high-dose ibuprofen is used, a single dose can be this large but it's given twice a day, not four times. Without a reason, this looks most like a units or frequency mix-up, and the risks of getting it wrong are serious: GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and heart problems.\n\n**Ways to move forward:**\n1. **Tell me the reason.** If there's a specific protocol, such as a research protocol with drug-level monitoring, let me know. I can enter the order with that reason in the note so pharmacy sees it when they verify.\n2. **Pick a standard dose** and I'll enter it now:\n   - 400 mg by mouth four times daily (1,600 mg/day)\n   - 600 mg by mouth four times daily (2,400 mg/day)\n   - 800 mg by mouth four times daily (3,200 mg/day)\n   - 1600 mg by mouth twice daily (3,200 mg/day, if the 1600 mg dose is what matters)\n3. **Have a pharmacist or attending sign off.** Once they've reviewed it, send me their name and the reason and I'll include both on the order.\n\nWhich would you like to do?"
      }
     ],
